                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Zen Bound 2 is a good idea that is well executed. What you see in the trailer is what you get. There is a lot of content to get busy with and there shouldn't be much to complain about if it wasn't for the challenge. \n\nThere isn't anything Zen about this game. It started nice initially but it kept getting worse with what it was throwing at you. You get wood carvings that became so complex that you have to pull your hair out at some point. I really tried to complete the game but I just couldn't anymore. \n\nThis game is only recommended to masochists. Avoid it if you're looking for something fair and relaxing. I spent around 14 hours and I've completed around/over 50% of the puzzles. \n\n",
